<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="using:RavensPort.UI.ViewModels"
             xmlns:conv="using:RavensPort.Converters"
             xmlns:models="using:RavensPort.Core.Models"
             xmlns:sys="using:System"
             x:Class="RavensPort.Views.CredentialsView"
             x:DataType="vm:CredentialsViewModel"
             Background="{StaticResource BgBrush}">
    <UserControl.Resources>
        <conv:CredentialStatusBrushConverter x:Key="StatusBrush"/>

        <sys:String x:Key="KindHelpText">What kind of secret this credential holds.

OAuth2 (user login)         — a grant authorized in your browser, refreshed automatically before it expires.
OAuth2 device code          — the provider shows a short code and you enter it on any device. Nothing comes back to this machine, so there is no redirect URI to register.
API key                     — a static key you paste in. No authorization flow, no expiry, nothing to refresh.
OAuth2 client credentials   — the app signs in as itself. No browser, no user; a token is minted from the client secret and re-minted when it ages out.
Google service account      — a downloaded key file signs for its own tokens. No browser, no user.

The last two are app logins: nothing to connect and nobody to consent, so a route can use them the moment they are saved. Every kind attaches to a route the same way.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="DeviceEndpointHelpText">Where a device code grant asks for its user code (RFC 8628).

Not the same address as the browser authorization endpoint — that one is a page for a browser, this one is called by the app and answers JSON. Providers publish them separately:

GitHub   https://github.com/login/device/code
Google   https://oauth2.googleapis.com/device/code

An OIDC provider lists it as "device_authorization_endpoint" in its discovery document.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="ServiceAccountHelpText">The whole JSON key file downloaded from Google Cloud Console.

IAM &amp; Admin → Service Accounts → your account → Keys → Add key → Create new key → JSON.

Paste it unedited, braces and all. It contains a private key, so it is stored in your password manager like any other secret and is never shown again after saving.

This is not the same file as an OAuth client secret — that one goes under the OAuth2 credential type.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="SubjectHelpText">Optional. The user this service account should act as (domain-wide delegation).

Leave blank for Google Cloud APIs, where the token should belong to the service account itself.

Set it for Workspace APIs — Gmail, Calendar, Drive — which act on a person's data. The account must first be granted the same scopes for your domain in the Admin console, under Security → API controls → Domain-wide delegation.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="ExtraParamsHelpText">Extra parameters added to the token request, written as   a=1&amp;b=2

This is where the parameter that decides what the token is actually for goes:

Auth0      audience=https://your-api/
Entra ID   resource=https://graph.microsoft.com

Values are percent-decoded once, so paste them exactly as the provider's documentation shows them.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="CredentialsInBodyHelpText">Where the client id and secret go on the token request.

Off — sent as an HTTP Basic Authorization header. This is what RFC 6749 has clients do by default.
On  — sent as client_id and client_secret form fields in the request body.

Providers disagree about which they accept, and one that wants the other answers with a bare "invalid_client" that says nothing about which half was wrong. If that is what you are seeing, try the opposite setting.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="DefaultPlacementHelpText">Where this credential's secret goes by default.

Used for two things: it is what the Test button sends, and it prefills the entry when you attach this credential to a route. A route can still override it.

OAuth2 tokens normally want   Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;
API keys normally want        X-Api-Key: &lt;key&gt;

Query-string placements are not offered — a secret in a URL is recorded by the upstream's access log, by every intermediary, and by browser history.</sys:String>

        <sys:String x:Key="TestEndpointHelpText">Optional. A URL that answers 200 to an authenticated GET.

Click Test to send one GET there with this credential attached and see what comes back. Only 200 counts as a pass: redirects are not followed, because following one would report a sign-in page as success.

Nothing else verifies a static API key — without this, the first sign of a typo is a 401 on a real request hours later.

Must be https (plain http is allowed only for localhost) — the secret is sent there.</sys:String>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">

        <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="0" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                      Padding="0,0,4,0">
            <StackPanel Margin="16">
            <TextBlock Text="Saved credentials" Classes="section" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>

            <TextBlock Classes="empty"
                       Text="No credentials yet — fill in the form below and choose Add credential."
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasNoCredentials}"/>

            <!--
                Every column is a template column, including the three that were DataGridTextColumn
                in WPF. Avalonia's DataGridTextColumn exposes only Font* and Foreground — it has no
                ElementStyle — and what those three columns used ElementStyle for was wrapping and
                vertical centring. A template with the TextBlock spelled out says the same thing
                without pretending the property exists.
            -->
            <DataGrid ItemsSource="{Binding Credentials}" AutoGenerateColumns="False" IsReadOnly="True"
                      Margin="0,0,0,12" IsVisible="{Binding HasCredentials}">
                <DataGrid.Columns>
                    <DataGridTemplateColumn Header="NAME" Width="120">
                        <DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:CredentialItemViewModel">
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                    </DataGridTemplateColumn>
                    <DataGridTemplateColumn Header="KIND" Width="90">
                        <DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:CredentialItemViewModel">
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding KindDisplay}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                    </DataGridTemplateColumn>
                    <!-- Scopes for an OAuth grant; for an API key there are none, so the column
                         carries the more useful fact — where the key goes by default. -->
                    <DataGridTemplateColumn Header="SCOPES / PLACEMENT" Width="*" MinWidth="160">
                        <DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:CredentialItemViewModel">
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ScopesDisplay}" TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                    </DataGridTemplateColumn>
                    <DataGridTemplateColumn Header="STATUS" Width="170">
                        <DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:CredentialItemViewModel">
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8" Margin="0,0,7,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                             Fill="{Binding StatusKind, Converter={StaticResource StatusBrush}}"/>
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding StatusDisplay}" TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                    </DataGridTemplateColumn>
                    <!-- 310 rather than WPF's 330. The fixed widths plus the star column's minimum
                         came to slightly more than the window, and Avalonia's grid clips the
                         overflow where WPF wrapped it — so the last button lost its right edge
                         instead of the row growing. Trimmed until the WrapPanel wraps again. -->
                    <DataGridTemplateColumn Header="ACTIONS" Width="310">
                        <DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:CredentialItemViewModel">
                                <WrapPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,4">
                                    <!-- Token operations. An API key has nothing to authorize and
                                         nothing to refresh, so they are hidden for one. The first
                                         button reads "Connect" only where a browser actually
                                         opens; an app login says "Get token", because calling it
                                         Connect promises a consent screen that never appears. -->
                                    <Button Content="{Binding AcquireButtonLabel}" Margin="2" Classes="ghost"
                                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.row.connect"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding HasToken}"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:CredentialsViewModel)DataContext).ConnectCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}"/>
                                    <!-- Disconnect only where clearing the token means something.
                                         An app login would mint another on the next request. -->
                                    <Button Content="Disconnect" Margin="2" Classes="ghost"
                                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.row.disconnect"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding CanDisconnect}"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:CredentialsViewModel)DataContext).DisconnectCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}"/>
                                    <Button Content="Refresh" Margin="2" Classes="ghost"
                                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.row.refresh"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding HasToken}"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:CredentialsViewModel)DataContext).RefreshNowCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}"/>
                                    <Button Content="Test" Margin="2" Classes="ghost"
                                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.row.test"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding CanTest}"
                                            ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource TestEndpointHelpText}"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:CredentialsViewModel)DataContext).TestCredentialCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}"/>
                                    <Button Content="Edit" Margin="2" Classes="ghost"
                                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.row.edit"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:CredentialsViewModel)DataContext).EditCredentialCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}"/>
                                    <Button Content="Delete" Margin="2" Classes="ghost"
                                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.row.delete"
                                            Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:CredentialsViewModel)DataContext).DeleteCredentialCommand}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}"/>
                                </WrapPanel>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </DataGridTemplateColumn.CellTemplate>
                    </DataGridTemplateColumn>
                </DataGrid.Columns>
            </DataGrid>

            <Border Classes="card" Margin="0,0,0,14">
                <StackPanel>
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding FormHeaderText}" Classes="section"/>

                    <!-- The kind is asked first because it decides which of the two blocks
                         below applies; almost nothing is shared between them. -->
                    <UniformGrid Columns="2" Rows="1" Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        <StackPanel Margin="0,0,6,0">
                            <TextBlock Text="Credential type" Classes="label"
                                       ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource KindHelpText}"/>
                            <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding Kinds}" SelectedValue="{Binding SelectedKind}"
                                      AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.kind"
                                      SelectedValueBinding="{Binding Kind}"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                      ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource KindHelpText}">
                                <ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:CredentialKindInfo">
                                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Label}"/>
                                    </DataTemplate>
                                </ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                            </ComboBox>
                        </StackPanel>
                        <StackPanel Margin="6,0,0,0">
                            <TextBlock Text="Name" Classes="label"/>
                            <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.name"
                                     Text="{Binding NewName}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </UniformGrid>

                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding KindBlurb}" Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,10"/>

                    <!-- ============ OAuth2 browser flow only ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsOAuthKind}">
                        <Border Background="{StaticResource PanelAltBrush}" BorderBrush="{StaticResource BorderBrush0}"
                                BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="4" Padding="10,8" Margin="0,0,0,12">
                            <StackPanel>
                                <TextBlock Text="Redirect URI" Classes="label"/>
                                <TextBox Text="{Binding RedirectUri, Mode=OneWay}" IsReadOnly="True"
                                         FontFamily="Consolas" Foreground="{StaticResource AccentBrush}"
                                         Background="Transparent" BorderThickness="0" Padding="0"
                                         Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding RedirectUriInfo}" Classes="hint"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Border>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- The preset picker serves both user-login flows. Its help text differs per
                         flow: the same provider enables and registers them differently, and the
                         redirect-URI advice above is meaningless for a device code. -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding UsesPreset}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Provider preset" Classes="label"/>
                        <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding Presets}" SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedPreset}"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                            <ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:OAuthProviderPreset">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}"/>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </ComboBox.ItemTemplate>
                        </ComboBox>
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding PresetHelpText}" Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,8"
                                   TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ client id + secret: the browser flow and the app login ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding UsesClientPair}">
                        <UniformGrid Columns="2" Rows="1" Margin="0,0,0,8">
                            <StackPanel Margin="0,0,6,0">
                                <TextBlock Text="Client ID" Classes="label"/>
                                <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.clientId"
                                         Text="{Binding NewClientId}"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <StackPanel Margin="6,0,0,0">
                                <!-- Labelled optional for the device flow: RFC 8628 exists for
                                     clients that cannot hold a secret, and most providers issue
                                     device codes to public ones. -->
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ClientSecretLabel}" Classes="label"/>
                                <TextBox PasswordChar="•" AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.clientSecret"
                                         Text="{Binding NewClientSecret}"/>
                                <TextBlock Text="Leave blank to keep the current secret" Classes="hint"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding IsEditing}" Margin="0,3,0,0"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </UniformGrid>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ device code ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsDeviceCodeKind}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Device authorization endpoint" Classes="label"
                                   ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource DeviceEndpointHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.deviceEndpoint" Text="{Binding NewDeviceAuthorizationEndpoint}"
                                 ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource DeviceEndpointHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,3,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Text="Where the user code is issued. Not the browser authorization endpoint — providers publish the two separately."/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ OAuth2 browser flow only: where the browser goes ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsOAuthKind}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Authority (OIDC discovery — leave blank for manual endpoints below)" Classes="label"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.authority" Text="{Binding NewAuthority}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>

                        <TextBlock Text="Authorization endpoint" Classes="label"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.authorizationEndpoint" Text="{Binding NewAuthorizationEndpoint}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- The token endpoint belongs to both grant kinds — it is the only endpoint an
                         app login has, since nothing ever opens a browser for one. -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding UsesTokenEndpoint}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Token endpoint" Classes="label"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.tokenEndpoint"
                                 Text="{Binding NewTokenEndpoint}" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsOAuthKind}">
                        <!-- Shown only for Google, the one provider whose flow actually reads this
                             flag. IdentityModel.OidcClient (GitHub/Nextcloud/Custom) always sends a
                             code_challenge and exposes no way to turn it off, so offering the
                             checkbox there advertised a setting that did nothing. -->
                        <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsPkceOptionApplicable}">
                            <CheckBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.pkce" Content="Use PKCE" IsChecked="{Binding NewUsesPkce}" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="Leave on unless your Google client is an older type that rejects PKCE."
                                       Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,10"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="PKCE is always used for this provider — the underlying OAuth library requires it."
                                   Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,10"
                                   IsVisible="{Binding IsPkceAlwaysOn}"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- Extra parameters serve both non-browser flows. There is no authorization
                         request to hang them on in either, so they ride on the request that
                         actually starts the flow. -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding UsesExtraParams}">
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding ExtraParamsLabel}" Classes="label"
                                   ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource ExtraParamsHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.extraParams" Text="{Binding NewExtraParams}"
                                 ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource ExtraParamsHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,3,0,10" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Text="a=1&amp;b=2 — e.g. audience=https://your-api/ for Auth0, or resource=… for Entra ID."/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ client credentials (app login) ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsClientCredentialsKind}">
                        <CheckBox Content="Send client credentials in request body"
                                  AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.secretInBody"
                                  IsChecked="{Binding NewSendClientCredentialsInBody}"
                                  ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource CredentialsInBodyHelpText}" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                        <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,10" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Text="Off sends them as an HTTP Basic header, which is the OAuth2 default. Turn this on if the provider answers 'invalid_client' for a client id and secret you know are right."/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ Google service account (app login) ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsServiceAccountKind}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Service account key (JSON)" Classes="label"
                                   ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource ServiceAccountHelpText}"/>
                        <!-- Multi-line, so it cannot be the masked box the other secrets use. It is
                             pasted once and never shown again — reopening the credential leaves
                             this blank, and blank means "keep the stored key". -->
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.serviceAccountJson" Text="{Binding NewServiceAccountJson}"
                                 AcceptsReturn="True" TextWrapping="NoWrap" Height="110"
                                 ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                                 ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                                 FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="11"
                                 ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource ServiceAccountHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,3,0,10" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Text="Paste the whole file from Google Cloud Console → IAM &amp; Admin → Service Accounts → Keys → Add key → JSON. Stored in your password manager and never redisplayed; leave blank to keep the current one."/>

                        <TextBlock Text="Impersonated user (optional — domain-wide delegation)" Classes="label"
                                   ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource SubjectHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.serviceAccountSubject" Text="{Binding NewServiceAccountSubject}"
                                 ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource SubjectHelpText}"/>
                        <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,3,0,10" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Text="Leave blank for Google Cloud APIs. Set it for Workspace APIs (Gmail, Calendar, Drive), which act on a person's data — the account needs domain-wide delegation granted for these scopes first."/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ scopes: every kind that asks a provider for anything ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding UsesScopes}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Scopes (comma or space separated)" Classes="label"/>
                        <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.scopes"
                                 Text="{Binding NewScopes}" Margin="0,0,0,10"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ API key ============ -->
                    <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsApiKeyKind}">
                        <TextBlock Text="API key" Classes="label"/>
                        <TextBox PasswordChar="•" AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.apiKey"
                                 Text="{Binding NewApiKey}"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="Stored encrypted and never redisplayed. Leave blank to keep the current key."
                                   Classes="hint" Margin="0,3,0,10"/>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ============ shared by both kinds ============ -->
                    <TextBlock Text="Default placement" Classes="label"
                               ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource DefaultPlacementHelpText}"/>
                    <UniformGrid Columns="3" Rows="1" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                        <StackPanel Margin="0,0,6,0">
                            <TextBlock Text="Placement" Classes="label"/>
                            <ComboBox ItemsSource="{Binding Placements}" SelectedItem="{Binding NewDefaultPlacement}"
                                      AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.placement"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                      ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource DefaultPlacementHelpText}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                        <StackPanel Margin="6,0">
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding DefaultParameterNameLabel}" Classes="label"/>
                            <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.parameter"
                                     Text="{Binding NewDefaultParameterName}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                        <StackPanel Margin="6,0,0,0">
                            <TextBlock Text="Value prefix" Classes="label"/>
                            <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.valuePrefix" Text="{Binding NewDefaultValuePrefix}"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </UniformGrid>
                    <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,10"
                               Text="{Binding DefaultInjectionSummary, StringFormat='Prefills routes as: {0}. A route can override it.'}"/>

                    <TextBlock Text="Test endpoint (optional)" Classes="label"
                               ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource TestEndpointHelpText}"/>
                    <TextBox AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.testEndpoint"
                             Text="{Binding NewTestEndpoint}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{StaticResource TestEndpointHelpText}"/>
                    <TextBlock Classes="hint" Margin="0,3,0,10"
                               Text="A URL answering 200 to an authenticated GET. Adds a Test button to this credential's row — the only way to check a static API key before a real request fails."/>
                    <TextBlock Text="⚠ Body placement cannot be tested — the test request is a GET, which has no body."
                               Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,10"
                               Foreground="{StaticResource ErrorBrush}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding IsUntestablePlacement}"/>

                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding SaveHintText}" Classes="hint" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>

                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                        <Button Content="{Binding SaveButtonLabel}" Width="140"
                                AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.save"
                                Command="{Binding SaveCredentialCommand}"/>
                        <Button Content="Cancel" Width="90" Margin="8,0,0,0" Classes="ghost"
                                AutomationProperties.AutomationId="credentials.editor.cancel"
                                Command="{Binding CancelEditCommand}"
                                IsVisible="{Binding IsEditing}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>

            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>

        <!-- Pinned footer: status stays visible instead of scrolling out of view. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="1" Classes="footer">
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding StatusMessage}" Classes="footer"/>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
